updateMenu(dt) {
  this.menuAngle += dt * 0.045;
  const car = this.playerCar;
  if (!car) return;
  const target = car.position.clone().add(new THREE.Vector3(0, 0.85, 0));
  const angle = this.menuAngle;
  const portrait = window.innerHeight > window.innerWidth * 1.1;
  const compact = window.innerHeight < 500;
  const distance = compact ? 12.8 : portrait ? 19.5 : 18.2;
  const desired = target.clone().add(new THREE.Vector3(
    Math.sin(angle) * distance,
    (compact ? 4.5 : portrait ? 6.6 : 6.2) + Math.sin(this.elapsed * 0.32) * 0.22,
    Math.cos(angle) * distance,
  ));
  this.camera.position.copy(desired);
  const look = target.clone().add(new THREE.Vector3(Math.cos(angle) * 1.1, 0.25, -Math.sin(angle) * 1.1));
  this.camera.lookAt(look);
  this.camera.fov = compact ? 50 : portrait ? 46 : 42;
  this.camera.updateProjectionMatrix();
  car.setNight(this.world.nightFactor);
  car.syncVisual();
}

Landscape gameplay at 844x390: mobile controls are hidden because `max-height:620 landscape` sets display none, and the later `hover:none coarse` rule sets display flex, but Playwright desktop context is not coarse, so hidden. On a real phone landscape, `hover:none` applies and controls show. But our test browser is not coarse even after resize. The screenshot shows no touch controls, but that's expected for desktop. However the mobile controls are needed for touch landscape; the CSS final rule should show. Fine. But the HUD speedo and minimap overlap? They are at bottom corners, fine. The car is small-ish but okay. The scene has black vertical poles from start gate at top, fine.

On real mobile landscape, controls will show at bottom and speedo/minimap bottom at 112px? The max-width 780 rules don't apply at 844 width, so speedo/minimap remain at bottom 26px, overlapping touch controls if shown. This is a problem for landscape phones with width >780 (e.g., 844x390). The `max-width:780px` rules don't apply, and landscape max-height rule hides mobile controls on non-coarse but coarse override shows them. Then speedo/minimap at bottom 26px overlap controls. We need add mobile HUD positioning in the landscape media query for coarse/short screens: move speedo/minimap up and size down, controls at bottom. Or simply add in max-height 620 landscape:
```
@media (max-height:620px) and (orientation:landscape) {
 .hud-bottom-left { bottom: calc(10px + safe); left: 14px; }
 .speedo { width: 96px; height: 96px; }
 .hud-bottom-right { bottom: calc(10px + safe); right: 14px; width: 96px; height: 96px; }
