 .touch-pedals { margin-right:0; }
}
```
But on desktop landscape 844x390, mobile controls should remain hidden (hover:hover), so don't set display flex in this media query. Instead use the existing `(hover:none) and (pointer:coarse)` rule at the end; we can add a landscape coarse query after it:
```
@media (hover:none) and (pointer:coarse) and (max-height:620px) and (orientation:landscape) {
 .hud-bottom-left { bottom: calc(104px + safe); }
 .speedo { width: 84px; height:84px; }
 ...
 .mobile-controls { display:flex; ...}
}
```
But CSS order: this should come after the hover:none rule. Or modify the hover:none rule to include short landscape overrides? Simpler add a new media query at the end.

Actually on a landscape phone 844x390, the HUD bottom corners at 26px will overlap controls at bottom 12px height 64. So we need move them up to ~100px or hide them. Could hide speedo/minimap in landscape mobile? Better keep but move up. At 390 height, speedo 84 at bottom 96 -> top 210, fine. Minimap 84 at bottom 96 -> top 210. Controls at bottom 12 height 64 -> top 314. Gap 20. Good.

